Health integrated care solution for the management of Metabolic-Associated Steatotic Liver Disease#🔵 Sonuç / Conclusions (Mavi)":[38,40],"#An AI-enabled mHealth integrated care solution for the management of Metabolic-Associated Steatotic Liver Disease#🔵 Sonuç / Conclusions (Mavi)#{1}":[39,40],"#An AI-enabled mHealth integrated care solution for the management of Metabolic-Associated Steatotic Liver Disease#🟠 Limitasyonlar (Turuncu)":[41,42]},"outlinks":[{"title":"Görüntüle","target":"zotero://select/library/items/LPRJTGXW","line":22},{"title":"Sayfa 1","target":"zotero://open-pdf/library/items/UXMEQUI8?page=1&annotation=4VK9FC8B","line":33},{"title":"Sayfa 1","target":"zotero://open-pdf/library/items/UXMEQUI8?page=1&annotation=ILHHZFQN","line":33},{"title":"Sayfa 2","target":"zotero://open-pdf/library/items/UXMEQUI8?page=2&annotation=7HTYY56F","line":33},{"title":"Sayfa 2","target":"zotero://open-pdf/library/items/UXMEQUI8?page=2&annotation=VRU8MDWC","line":33},{"title":"Sayfa 2","target":"zotero://open-pdf/library/items/UXMEQUI8?page=2&annotation=YQSPB5W8","line":33},{"title":"Sayfa 6","target":"zotero://open-pdf/library/items/UXMEQUI8?page=6&annotation=4ZHBGFYW","line":36},{"title":"Sayfa 6","target":"zotero://open-pdf/library/items/UXMEQUI8?page=6&annotation=G9ZLTJX9","line":36},{"title":"Sayfa 1","target":"zotero://open-pdf/library/items/UXMEQUI8?page=1&annotation=44B2ZIHC","line":39},{"title":"Sayfa 1","target":"zotero://open-pdf/library/items/UXMEQUI8?page=1&annotation=CY6YBKMF","line":39},{"title":"Sayfa 6","target":"zotero://open-pdf/library/items/UXMEQUI8?page=6&annotation=A2C6RMQ5","line":39},{"title":"Sayfa 6","target":"zotero://open-pdf/library/items/UXMEQUI8?page=6&annotation=WWBUKC8B","line":39}],"metadata":{"Title":"An AI-enabled mHealth integrated care solution for the management of Metabolic-Associated Steatotic Liver Disease","Authors":"Simone Kresevic, Mauro Giuffrè, Carlo Moretto, Lorenzo Zucchini, Aleksandar Miladinović, Maria Bongiovanni, Alberto Bortolotto, Marina Discipio, Alex Buoite Stella, Agostino Accardo, Lory Saveria Crocè, Miloš Ajčević","Year":2025,"DOI":"10.1109/EMBC58623.2025.11253032","Nitelik":null,"Alan":null,"Konu":null,"AI_Methodology":null,"Layer_Focus":null,"Model_Asamasi":null,"Proposed_Tool":null,"Methods":"We aimed to design and develop a patient-centered, mHealthenabled integrated care application (named AI-MASLD) that empowers patients and enhances their management through a human-in-the-loop AI approach.The developed system features a patient-centered mobile app with gamified self-management tools for diet and physical activity tracking as well as stress monitoring. Healthcare professionals have access to a dashboard with role-specific tools, allowing physicians, dietitians, and physiotherapists to provide tailored care and approve AI-generated recommendationEarly prototypes were regularly shared with clinicians and general user to identify usability issues, refine interface design, and optimize functionalities such as gamification, recommendation clarity, and overall user experience.The server side is supported by a robust cloud infrastructure responsible for processing data and executing AI-driven decision support, thereby enabling a seamless integration of advanced functionalitiesData processing and AI layer: a Large Language Model (e.g., Llama 3.2 3B) in the role of an AI-agent allows interaction with the patient data, patient inputs and could also be integrated with ML algorithms.  It orchestrates data processing to identify trends and risks, and generate explainable, personalized recommendations","Findings":"In this study, we designed and developed AI-MASLD, an AI-powered mHealth platform aimed at enhancing MASLD management by integrating human-in-the-loop AI, decision support, and gamification strategies. By fostering collaboration among primary care, hospital, and social care professionals, AI-MASLD offers an integrated care solution that enhances patient rehabilitation and engagement.By adopting a human-in-the-loop approach, the platform ensures that AI-generated recommendations are validated by healthcare professionals, improving the safety and relevance of clinical interventions.","Conclusions":"In conclusion, the developed mHealth solution could represent a promising tool for the management of MASLD, integrating cutting-edge AI technology with personalized carhe proposed system could serve as a valuable tool to empower MASLD patients and enhance their management and rehabilitation. By bridging healthcare professionals’ expertise with patient data, the platform aims to significantly improve patient outcomes, engagement, and adherence, while fostering a collaborative care environment.A key innovation of AI-MASLD is its AI-powered decision support system, which generates personalized, explainable recommendations that dynamically adapt to changes in a patient’s condition. The integration of a human-in-the-loop approach, wherein physicians validate AI-generated insights, further enhances the safety, reliability, and clinical relevance of the interventions.AI-MASLD fosters multidisciplinary collaboration among hepatologists, physiotherapists, dietitians, psychologists, and primary care providers, creating a comprehensive and patient-centered care ecosystem. Through gamification, social engagement, and augmented intelligence, the platform aims to improve adherence and health outcomes. While promising, future clinical studies are necessary to validate its effectiveness and facilitate its integration into the patient rehabilitation pathway.","Limitations":"","User_Notes":""},"task_lines":[],"tasks":{},"codeblock_ranges":[],"last_embed":{"hash":"2fgn1y","at":1774939548230}},"smart_blocks:Augmented Dietitian Okunmuşlar/kresevicAIenabledMHealthIntegrated2025.md#---frontmatter---": {"path":null,"embeddings":{"TaylorAI/bge-micro-v2":{"vec":[-0.03587219,-0.00616912,0.02998402,0.00258599,-0.04102597,-0.01396896,-0.00868712,0.04904823,0.04426147